# DRAFT: nothing has been released yet. The version, date and DOI are filled in at release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WarnText, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "WarnText: a research corpus of the public emergency alert messages sent in the United States"
abstract: >-
  WarnText is a corpus of the public emergency alert messages sent in the United States through
  the Integrated Public Alert and Warning System since June 2012 (Wireless Emergency Alerts,
  Emergency Alert System messages and others), one row per message with its sender, time,
  place, channel and full text, and with updates and cancellations linked to the alert they
  follow.
authors:
  - family-names: Kraishan
    given-names: Obada
    affiliation: "College of Media and Communication, Texas Tech University"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/obadaKraishan/warntext"
keywords:
  - emergency alerts
  - Wireless Emergency Alerts
  - crisis communication
  - risk communication
  - communication research
  - dataset
